Notes:

- Text takes a dictionary like t2c={"world": RED} to color part of the text by matching the words.
- Circle's docs page does not say what radius=None turns into. Pass a radius yourself.
- Tex wraps your text in a center environment, and MathTex wraps it in align\*. MathTex is the one for formulas.
- Axes: the docs page does not say what x\_range=None and y\_range=None turn into, so pass your own ranges.
- NumberPlane: if x\_length and y\_length are left unset, one unit on each axis equals one Manim unit.
- ThreeDAxes: the docs say depth and gloss currently do nothing.
- The 3D objects (Cube, Sphere, Cone, Cylinder, Torus, Prism, Surface) take extra styling through \*\*kwargs. Their pages do not list which ones.

## 3. Animations and self.play()

An animation only runs when it is passed to self.play(...). Creating one on its own line does nothing.

### Options every animation shares (Animation base class)

| Parameter | Default | What it does |
| --- | --- | --- |
| run\_time | 1.0 | Duration in seconds (some animations set their own default) |
| rate\_func | smooth | Speed curve over time. linear gives a steady speed |
| lag\_ratio | 0.0 | Delay between submobjects, as a fraction of the animation |
| reverse\_rate\_function | False | Plays the speed curve backwards |
| name | None | Label shown while rendering |
| remover | False | If True, removes the mobject from the scene afterwards |
| introducer | False | Marks the animation as one that adds its mobject to the scene u|
| suspend\_mobject\_updating | True | Pauses the mobject's updaters dring the animation |

